---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="NeuroPolicy Cognita sits at the intersection of behavioural science, public policy and markets." active="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <span class="label">About</span>
      <h1>Where disciplines meet decisions</h1>
      <p class="lede">NeuroPolicy Cognita sits at the intersection of behavioural science, public policy and markets.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="about">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Most big outcomes, whether a market crash, an election swing or a brand's rise, come down to millions of small human decisions. NeuroPolicy Cognita exists to study those decisions across fields that rarely talk to each other.</p>
        <p>Finance explains how people price risk. Politics explains how societies choose rules. Marketing explains how preferences are shaped. Read together, they give a sharper picture of why people act the way they do, and how institutions can work with that behaviour instead of against it.</p>
        <p>That is why every essay here is tagged with more than one lens. A piece on luxury pricing is also a piece on status psychology; a piece on geopolitics is also a piece on trade and capital. Follow the tags and you will find the connections.</p>
        <h2>Open to contributors</h2>
        <p>This is not a single-author blog. Students, practitioners and researchers are welcome to pitch essays, case studies and short analyses. If you have a well-argued idea about how people decide, it belongs here.</p>
        <p><a class="btn" href={url('/contact/')}>Pitch an essay</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="principles">
        <div><b>Evidence first</b><p>Claims are tied to data, studies or cases the reader can check.</p></div>
        <div><b>Across fields</b><p>Every piece borrows at least one idea from outside its home discipline.</p></div>
        <div><b>Readable</b><p>Rigour without jargon. If it cannot be explained clearly, it is not ready.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .about{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(32px,6vw,96px);align-items:start}
  .prose{display:grid;gap:18px;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:62ch}
  .prose h2{font-size:var(--s4);margin-top:20px}
  .prose .btn{font-family:var(--body)}
  .principles{display:grid;gap:28px}
  .principles div{border-top:2px solid var(--accent);padding-top:14px}
  .principles b{display:block;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:400;font-size:1.35rem;margin-bottom:6px}
  .principles p{color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem}
  @media (max-width:820px){.about{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
